//api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122137","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122137","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122137.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122137.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/9829#issue-2318338949\r\n\r\nImplements the ability to point a project from the project list to a new project location. Intended especially to relocate projects which are marked as missing, being more intuitive than removing and re-adding it.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nRelocation can always be triggered via a context menu option or when trying to open a missing project. It turned out to be technically challenging to conditionally disable or remove the context menu option when right-clicking a non-missing project, so it is alyways possible. The use-case is there anyways (Moving a project while the list is opened does not update the item as missing, which would otherwise prevent the option from being useable and require a restart).","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122137/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122137/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}